<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Évora</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ebora, Evora</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Évora is a city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a> region of southern Portugal. As Roman Ebora Liberalitas Julia it was a municipality of Lusitania, and its well-preserved Roman temple of the 1st century CE is among the best-known Roman monuments in Portugal. It was later a frequent residence of the Portuguese kings, and its historic centre is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/evora.jpg" alt="Évora" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Philipp from Darmstadt, Germany · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pra%C3%A7a_de_Giraldo,_Evora_(10250693386)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
